Source package: gnome-session

leave-scope-to-glib.patch
    Lets gnome-session leave the scope of an application it starts at login to GLib, when the
    platform data of GLib's "launched" signal names one as "systemd-unit". The GLib of
    patches/glib2.0/ puts the application into that scope before it starts, so a request of
    gnome-session for the scope is redundant: systemd creates the scope for whichever request it
    receives first and refuses the other, which logs a warning in the journal when it is
    gnome-session's. Drop the patch together with patches/glib2.0/scope-before-exec.patch.

    The request is made in app_launched in gnome-session/gsm-util.c. The patch adds no test, as
    gnome-session's tests do not launch applications.

    Check by hand after a rebuild and a new login:

      journalctl --user -b | grep 'Could not create transient scope'
                                  should find nothing

restart-dbus-replace-queued-jobs.patch
    Lets gnome-session stop the session bus at the end of the session also while the start of a service which needs
    the bus waits in a queued job. gnome-session-restart-dbus.service stops dbus.service then, so that the next login
    starts a new bus. gnome-session asks systemd for the stop with the job mode "fail", which systemd refuses when the
    stop conflicts with a queued job, and the next login then uses the old bus. Such a job is queued when a D-Bus
    activation during the shutdown starts a service: Desktop Icons NG starts its process again while GNOME Shell shuts
    down (reported as desktop-icons-ng issue 395), which starts xdg-desktop-portal, whose start job stays queued, as
    its GNOME backend cannot start once the graphical session has ended. The patch stops the bus with the job mode
    "replace", with which systemd cancels such a job instead.

    The stop is made in do_restart_dbus in tools/gnome-session-ctl.c. The session test restart-bus in tests/session/
    queues such a job before logging out and checks that the bus is restarted. Not proposed upstream. Drop the patch
    once gnome-session stops the bus without failing on a queued job.
